============================================================
qemu-minimal emulated GPU guest  ({{ ansible_hostname }})
============================================================
Kernel:       {{ ansible_kernel }}
ROCm prefix:  {{ rocm_setup_therock_prefix | default('unknown') }}
hsa-snoop:    v{{ rocjitsu_setup_tools_hsa_snoop_version }}  (installed, services disabled)
============================================================

Two services are disabled on this guest to prevent GPU lockup:

hsa-snoop (.service and -prometheus.service)
  hsa-snoop holds trace_pipe open. On an emulated GPU the
  scratch segment is served to exactly one process at a time;
  a background collector wedges the device for every workload
  that follows. Symptom: dispatch hangs waiting for scratch.

gpuagent
  gpuagent calls amdsmi for temperature/clock/utilisation.
  The emulated gfx1250 returns AMDSMI_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED,
  causing gpuagent to assertion-fail and wedge /dev/kfd.
  Symptom: next process gets -EBUSY opening /dev/kfd.

Do not re-enable either service on this guest.
============================================================
